"Times we used to fight each other\nThe era was of never-show-care\n\nYes we did had many fights\nThere were no wrongs and no rights\nAll we knew this was love lang\nMild roast was a love shaped slang\n\nTimes we thought to separate\nTimes we used to irritate \nTimes we made each other bait\nTimes our mother scold us great\n\nYes the times changed\nSeparation erupted love\nThe need we had for each other\nDeep inside but not exterior\n\nNow we thrive to live together\nChances we get to talk to each other \nStill we don't know what to talk about\nAnd that's where comes our mother\n\nLike a bridge between attracting bodies\nBound by chains and not coming closer\nThe bridge help us communicate more\nAnd day by day, we're getting better"